Attorney general-elected. 25LSO-0396, 1.0
FISCAL NOTE
The fiscal impact, in the form of potential increased expenditures, is
indeterminable.
Under this bill, the Attorney General is no longer required to commence an action
when directed by the Governor, the Supreme Court, or the Wyoming Legislature. The
Attorney General’s Office indicates this change could have a fiscal impact if the
elected Attorney General decides not to commence an action and outside counsel is
hired by the Governor, the Supreme Court, or the Wyoming Legislature.
